    <kbr:dokumenSumber>SRC_EXT_002</kbr:dokumenSumber>
    <kbr:identifierSumber>Abstract</kbr:identifierSumber>
    <kbr:kutipanSumber>Disease development is strongly associated with temperatures of 26–30 °C, high relative humidity, and prolonged leaf wetness, conditions commonly observed during the rainy season in tropical agroecosystems.</kbr:kutipanSumber>
    <kbr:kutipanNormalisasi>Disease development is strongly associated with temperatures of 26–30 °C, high relative humidity, and prolonged leaf wetness, conditions commonly observed during the rainy season in tropical agroecosystems.</kbr:kutipanNormalisasi>
